            "A full reading session, timed and annotated — the method applied to a realistic diff (a \"download my data\" endpoint the previous prompt specs produced).\n\n```\nMINUTE 0-3 · Contract first (before touching the body)\n  Written down: GET /api/export → 200 text/csv | 401 | 422? | errors as envelope;\n  side effects: reads progress + profile; logs one info event; no writes.\n  QUESTION TO ANSWER: does the diff match this? Any writes I didn't sanction?\n\nMINUTE 3-8 · Tests read first (they exist — 4 of them)\n  ✓ own-data-only test asserts 200 + header row + 3 rows  (criterion 1)\n  ✓ cross-tenant test asserts 403                        (criterion 2 — the matrix cell!)\n  ✗ NOTHING for: empty account, CSV metacharacters, 5k rows/streaming\n  → three criteria untested. Will check implementation handles them anyway.\n\nMINUTE 8-14 · Happy path trace\n  requireSession → loadProgress(userId) → map to rows → serialize → respond.\n  Matches contract. No writes seen. ✓. One oddity noted: `buildCsv(rows)` is\n  a NEW local helper…\n\nMINUTE 14-24 · Edge hunt (the meat)\n  empty       : rows=[] → header-only response ✓ (found in code, not tests)\n  metachars   : buildCsv wraps in quotes & doubles internal `\"` ✓ BUT…\n                cell starting with `=` is passed through raw → CSV-INJECTION\n                (the backend course's exact warning) — DEFECT 1, security-adjacent\n  5k rows     : joins the whole CSV into one string before responding →\n                memory spike; spec said stream — DEFECT 2 (spec violation)\n  null fields : profile.name ?? \"\" ✓ ; progress.pct undefined → cell \"undefined\"\n                (literal word) — DEFECT 3 (the NaN-family, at the CSV layer)\n  errors      : AppError envelope ✓; catch-all → 500 with requestId ✓\n\nMINUTE 24-27 · Seams & grep\n  validation  : n/a (GET only) ✓\n  error helper: YOUR AppError ✓ used, not invented\n  logging     : YOUR logger ✓ one info event, no payloads (allow-list respected)\n  new helpers : buildCsv — grep: no existing CSV helper → justified. But it\n                duplicated 3 lines of date formatting from format.ts → DEFECT 4\n                (near-duplicate seam miss; trivial, but it's how divergence starts)\n  hallucination check: streaming via Response constructor + Readable.toWeb —\n                docs opened, API exists ✓ (the one unfamiliar call, verified)\n\nMINUTE 27-30 · Verdict & feedback\n  4 defects: 1 security-ish (must fix), 1 spec violation (must fix),\n  2 quality (fix in same pass — they're 2 minutes each).\n  Return NOT ship: \"cause-first on the CSV `=` cell (pasted trace context),\n  stream per spec, pct → format helper, reuse format.ts for dates; then add\n  tests for empty + metachars + 5,000 rows.\"\n\nREAD TIME: 30 min for 180 lines + 4 tests. Defects found: 4 (1 would have been\na real security finding in code review of a human's code — the bar is the same).\n\n── Next generation (iteration 2, 12 minutes later) ──\n  New diff: 34 lines (fixes + tests). Same contract first (30 sec), tests\n  (2 min), edges (5 min), seams (2 min), verdict: ship. \n  40 minutes total for a correct, tested, convention-following feature —\n  generation included. The economics work *because* each iteration was small\n  and each return was specific (defects, not \"meh\").\n```\n\n**What the session demonstrates**: the contract-first habit made every later check a comparison instead of an exploration; **tests-first told me what they *didn't* cover**, which directed the edge hunt (three untested criteria → all three found handled-or-not in code); the seam-grep caught the kind of thing that never shows up in demo runs; the unfamiliar-API check was the *one* hallucination-risk call and it passed — done anyway, because \"usually right\" is not a verification; and the *specific* return (defect + evidence + test request) made iteration two fast. Contrast the failure mode this avoids: skim → ship → CSV injection found by a user → incident. Thirty minutes is the insurance premium, and the reading lesson's method is the policy.",
